        "content": "<p>Hey, I've been trying out the new <code>autoTry</code> features (thanks for adding <code>sorry</code> support!) and they keep suggesting to use the theorem to solve itself:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">autoTry</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">onSorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">warning: declaration uses `sorry`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">---</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: Try this:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [apply] exact _root_.foo</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
